Subject: [PATCH 0069] nmxtrace: GPU interrupt heartbeat in NVRAM and an interrupt-storm guard

Wildcat Lake test starts 11-13: the panel modeset succeeds, then the whole Mac freezes a few seconds later, each
time at a different step of the attach thread (IOFramebuffer start, registerService, registerPowerDriver), with
nothing of the start saved to the log. Something asynchronous takes the machine down; an interrupt the 6.14 display
code does not acknowledge on display 30.02 (firing without end) is a prime suspect.

- xnu/nmx_pci.cpp: with nmxtrace set, from the first GPU interrupt a heartbeat writes
  "t=<s> irqs=<total> rate=<last second>" to NVRAM (nullmoth-gpu-hb) every 2 s for 60 s, and more than 50000
  interrupts within a second disables the interrupt source (logged and noted in nullmoth-gpu-hb) so the Mac survives.
- xnu/nmx_kext.cpp: nmx_xnu_nvram_note(key, text); the breadcrumb uses it.
- bsdcompat/src/nmx_trace.c: nmx_trace_get_level().
Read after a start with:  nvram nullmoth-gpu-hb

Applies on top of 0051-0068.

